    {
      "id": "p0099-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This is a groaningly simple pun on the word “bark” – as in “tree bark” – and the dog-themed English idiom, “its bark is worse than its bite”.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.0919825,
          0.3271429,
          0.7143977,
          0.3642857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0919825,
          0.3271429,
          0.7143977,
          0.3642857
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "这是个简单得让人想叹气的双关：bark 既指“树皮”，也指“狗叫”，而 its bark is worse than its bite 是一句形容“叫得凶、咬得轻”的英语习语。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
